  "query_preview": "..Latest WV/IR satellite imagery shows mostly clear \nskies as a very weak trough is moving from west to east across the \nstate. Less wind today with just some afternoon gustiness as highs \nremain about 3 to 7 degrees above normal. \n\nFor this weekend into early next week, our weather is going to be \ninfluenced by a stronger dry trough swinging through to our north. \nThe main impacts for us will be the wind and resulting fire weather \nconcerns. Winds on Saturday will become breezy in the afternoon with \nsustained southwest winds of 15-20 mph and gusts up to around 30 \nmph. While wind speeds will remain below critical levels Saturday, \nelevated to near critical fire weather conditions are expected \nSaturday afternoon. \n\nThe aforementioned trough will swing through to our north Sunday \ninto Monday and this will be the period for the strongest winds \nacross our forecast area. Current indications are that Sunday will \nbe the day with the most widespread stronger winds across a broad \nswath of our forecast area with sustained southwest winds of 20-30 \nmph and gusts 35-45 mph. Winds will be similar Monday south and east \nof Tucson. We're still on track for potential fire weather headlines \nSunday and perhaps Monday as well. Otherwise, with the trough \nswinging through that will bring in cooler temperatures Sunday and \nMonday with highs 2 to 6 degrees below normal. \n\nThereafter, benign weather for the rest of next week as dry \nconditions continue with less wind (typical afternoon breezes). \nTemperatures will warm to near normal levels during this period.",
